# Cross-spec / cross-production constant consistency (machine-checked by verify.sh).
#
# Format (pipe-delimited):
#   spec|<SpecName>|<ConstantName>|<ExpectedValue>
#   prod|<FilePath>|<ExactDeclarationSubstring>
#
# verify.sh asserts that the spec declares `pure val <ConstantName> = <Value>`
# and that the production file contains the exact substring, so drift on either
# side (a model constant or a production constant) fails the gate.
#
# Semantics note: attempt/retry counting differs per spec — `SynthesisRetry`
# `MAX_RETRIES` counts retries (attempts = 1 + MAX_RETRIES), while `Download`
# `MAX_ATTEMPTS` and `StartupResources` `MAX_RETRY` bound total attempts. Do not
# assume a shared meaning; see STATE_TRACEABILITY.md "Cross-spec consistency".
spec|Daemon|MAX_RETRY|10
spec|MCPServer|MAX_ATTEMPTS|10
spec|System|MAX_CONNECT_ATTEMPTS|10
spec|SynthesisRetry|MAX_RETRIES|2
spec|System|MAX_SYNTH_RETRIES|2
spec|Download|MAX_ATTEMPTS|3
spec|StartupResources|MAX_RETRY|3
spec|McpRequestLifecycle|MAX_CONCURRENT|4
spec|DaemonServer|MAX_IN_FLIGHT|32
spec|DaemonSynthesisPath|MAX_IN_FLIGHT|32
prod|src/infrastructure/daemon/mod.rs|MAX_CONNECT_ATTEMPTS: u32 = 10
prod|src/interface/mcp_server/tools/text_to_speech.rs|MCP_DAEMON_MAX_RETRIES: u32 = 2
prod|src/interface/mcp_server/server/runtime.rs|MAX_CONCURRENT_TOOL_HANDLERS: usize = 4
prod|src/infrastructure/daemon/server.rs|MAX_CONCURRENT_CLIENTS: usize = 32
